00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Nicholas Sanders: Um…

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:49.000
Nicholas Sanders: Yeah, we're just a little bit curious about what kind of companies that you've seen success with, what kind of companies that you work with, what kind of, you know, wedding vendors that you are focused in on. Do you have anybody else in Dallas? Do you have any use cases, or sorry, success cases you can share with us?

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.000
Nicholas Sanders: Um… anything like that?

00:02:52.000 --> 00:03:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Definitely, yes. So we work with wedding pros all over, mostly throughout the United States. So a lot of venues, photographers, several planners, some entertainment companies.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Inside the ads accelerators themselves, I typically see planners and photographers joining for the most part. They seem to kind of be a little bit more like on the tech savvy side, kind of like, you know, already doing their own things like with their own content and really having the desire to.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Whitney Hodges: learn how to make ads work for their businesses with the right support in their corner.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.000
Nicholas Sanders: What do you…

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:44.000
Nicholas Sanders: What do you mean when you say inside the ads accelerators program? What do you mean by that? What does that mean?

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:04:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Sure, yeah, so we work with clients in two different capacities, right? We have our ads accelerators, which are meant to, um, get you started on the right foot with your advertising. So, we're helping you launch your Google Ads, we're helping you launch your Meta Ads.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:18.000
Whitney Hodges: We're giving you, uh, support and resources to see success with those ads, but you're a very active participant in that, right? So, you know, most people who join, um, that program, um, they're… they're wanting to be able to.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:37.000
Whitney Hodges: learn how everything works. They're not necessarily wanting to be locked into a long-term, ongoing retainer with an agency. They want that help and support for the initial commitment, so when you do the Ads Accelerator Bundle, it's 6 months of that initial support, and then from there, want the flexibility to be able to.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:50.000
Whitney Hodges: handle things on their own, or then maybe at that time, kind of, like, you know, make a decision to work together in a deeper capacity. So that's kind of, like, the first track, right, that we work with clients on. The latter…

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.000
Nicholas Sanders: So it's a course.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:05:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Kind of. Um, I would call it more of a hybrid program, because there are… it entails a lot of different things, right? So, there… there is some curriculum in there, there are some videos, you know, that we would want you to, um, to watch and understand, to really kind of understand our.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:26.000
Whitney Hodges: philosophy, our strategy, learn about the foundations for success with ads, but there's a ton of hands-on support beyond that, right? So, you know, for running successful Google Ads and Meta Ads campaigns, one of the biggest components is having.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Whitney Hodges: a landing page that is optimized for conversions, right? You need somewhere to send that ad traffic that's going to turn into inquiries, right? So, inside the Ads Accelerators, we share examples of a lot of great landing pages, we give you, kind of, pointers on, you know, what your own landing page should.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:06:04.000
Whitney Hodges: contain and should look like, and then kind of leave it up to you to build that page for yourself, right, on your website. You can then share that with us, submit it to us, and we give you personalized feedback. So that's kind of just an example. Kind of same thing goes, like, on the meta ad side, right? Giving you lots of examples of.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:21.000
Whitney Hodges: what makes really great ad creative, great ad copy, and then you get to tap into us for our personalized feedback on anything that you put together for the ads. But the part of those programs that is completely done for you is that we have access to your.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:37.000
Whitney Hodges: ads accounts, right? Or if you don't already have ad accounts, we help you get those set up the right way, and we actually go into your ad accounts, and we're launching the Google Ads for you, we're launching the Meta Ads for you. Um, and then, you know, you have access to us to ask.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:56.000
Whitney Hodges: questions about, you know, how things are going with the ads. There's office hours that happen once a week for both Google Ads and Meta Ads, where you can get… Jacqueline and Carmen, they're our ads experts. You can get their eyes on your accounts, um, in… in real time, right? Make tweaks or changes in real time to optimize things based on.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:11.000
Whitney Hodges: on how things are going. Um, yeah, so that's kind of the ads accelerator in a nutshell, versus a program that we have that's called Elevate, which is a fully done-for-you program, where we.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:30.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, again, we're running Google Ads, we're running Meta Ads, we're also building the full funnel for you in our lead management platform called Lead Lock. So, it's where we're setting up an ads traffic landing page for you, email and text nurture sequences to nurture your leads.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:46.000
Whitney Hodges: as they come in, you know, booking funnels for people to book sales consultations on your calendar and nurture them leading into those appointments. So, like I said, that's kind of completely done for you.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:08:06.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, and that is more of, you know, a long-term, ongoing agency retainer. Um, you know, we have clients that we've worked with in that capacity, you know, going on, like, 6, 7 years now, sort of thing, right? So, most people that sign on for Elevate, um, are really looking for that.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:22.000
Whitney Hodges: long-term partnership. They're not necessarily looking to learn things themselves or add another thing onto their plates. And inside Elevate, the majority of clients that we work with are venues, but we've definitely worked with.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:39.000
Whitney Hodges: uh, you know, photographers in that capacity as well. Um, and as far as your question about, you know, um, you know, success stories or, um, case studies, I'm, I'm happy to, uh, send you more on that. Um, you know, we, we have kind of a, a packet of some information on.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:48.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, different things that we've seen as far as, uh, case studies, success stories across the board, and, um, I'd be happy to send that your way.

