Ava Hopkins: Yeah.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:16:12.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, perfect. Okay, so Elevate is our full-service premium ads management program. Um, it's also backed by, um, automation, so, you know, email and text automations and lead management inside of our platform.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.000
Whitney Hodges: Lead lock.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:16.000
Whitney Hodges: So, um…

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:39.000
Whitney Hodges: Our team, our name, Wedding Industry Ads, we do specialize only in working with businesses in the wedding industry, right? Because it's different than if you're just a local business owner with repeat clientele or versus what's going on in the online business space, right? There are tried and true funnels that we see that are.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:56.000
Whitney Hodges: working for, um, for wedding pros these days. So that is really what we focus in on. The strategic advertising on both Google and Meta that's gonna drive more qualified traffic your way, plus building a seamless inquiry system for you inside of LeadLock to help convert more of those leads.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:57.000
Nicholas Sanders: Okay.

00:16:56.000 --> 00:17:14.000
Whitney Hodges: into consultations for you. So, um, to get things started, we have a very comprehensive onboarding process. So, um, you know, this will entail some, you know, collaboration from you and time on your end as well.

00:17:14.000 --> 00:17:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Typically, within the, um, the, the first, uh, two weeks of working together, um, we try to, like, knock out four meetings, um, right off of, of the bat, right? So about, like, four hours, um, in total. Even before that meeting takes place, we'll have you give to us a pretty in-depth.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:45.000
Whitney Hodges: onboarding questionnaire for us to really help understand your business, your ideal clients, your goals, right? Kind of like where you are at with things currently.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:18:03.000
Whitney Hodges: Then what those onboarding calls are going to look like when we start working together, the first call is more just about, like, setting expectations and also getting all of, like, the tech connections out of the way, right? Because in order to be able to run these ads on your behalf, we need access to your Google ad account, access to.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:11.000
Whitney Hodges: your Meta business portfolio and Meta ad account. So we knock all of that out on the first call.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:28.000
Whitney Hodges: Following that, we're going to have an in-depth messaging and positioning interview. So this is where, beyond even the onboarding questionnaire, we have a pretty lengthy discussion, again, to understand, you know, your unique value proposition.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:45.000
Whitney Hodges: who your ideal client is, how things, you know, compare to your competitors, all of that, right? We want to dig deep so that we have all of that information to build a high converting ads traffic landing page for you, as well as, you know, really strong.

00:18:45.000 --> 00:19:01.000
Whitney Hodges: add copy and and and add creatives. We know that the messaging is the most important part to really be able to draw in and speak to your ideal clients. Of course, you know the targeting and objectives, and all of that is important, too, right? But without.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:07.000
Whitney Hodges: strong messaging, things are just going to fall flat. So that's why we spend so much time there.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:26.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, also as part of the onboarding process, there's going to be a LeadLock kickoff call. So, this would be a call with, um, Danielle, who's our LeadLock implementation specialist, um, to be able to, you know, get you connected to that platform as far as, you know.

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:44.000
Whitney Hodges: email, calendars, um, things like that, kind of discuss with you, like, the overall roadmap of how we typically will set it up for, um, for our clients, but then it's all totally customizable, right? Like, we're not dropping you into, like, a cookie cutter or, like, plug-and-play system. It really is customized.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:20:03.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, for… for how you do business. Um, the fourth onboarding call is your ad strategy call. So, we're gonna go over the customized plan that we have for you, for your Meta ads, and for your Google ads, share all of the keyword research that we've done.

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:19.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, and basically get your stamp of approval for your Google Ads to go live. Um, from there, our team is really kind of, like, working in the background on building all of these assets out for you, right? Your ads traffic landing page, um, email and text.

00:20:19.000 --> 00:20:34.000
Whitney Hodges: nurture sequences, um, ad copy, and creative for your, um, your meta ads. Um, for the meta ads, we run what we call a full funnel of ads. So, there are gonna be different campaigns.

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:51.000
Whitney Hodges: Top of funnel to reach completely cold audiences, different campaigns, um, for, uh, you know, specifically optimized for conversions to get, you know, more inquiries in your pipeline, and then bottom of funnel retargeting ads. So, you know, there are different objectives that are going to be.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:21:12.000
Whitney Hodges: in place for each stage of the funnel, different types of copy and creative that are really needed, right? Depending on where people are in their customer journey and what we are wanting to say to them, right? So as all of those assets are getting completed by our team, we're then sending them over to you, right, for your review and your stamp of approval.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:28.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, and as you're approving things, then things are, you know, getting rolled out, um, from there, in terms of the ad shopping landing page, you know, launching, uh, the, the meta ads. Typically, we're, you know, launching top to bottom, right? Top of funnel ads go out first, then conversion ads, and then bottom of funnel.

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, and then, um, you know, when everything is approved on your end and has been tested and troubleshooted on our end on the lead lock side, um, that there's going to be, like, a final, um, implementation call for… for that.

00:21:45.000 --> 00:22:00.000
Whitney Hodges: Right? Because not only is the ads traffic landing page going to be live, but we recommend utilizing Leadlock for all of your inquiries, right, that are coming through organically. So, you know, we would want to embed the Leadlock form on your website, so all of that.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:15.000
Whitney Hodges: can flow through there. And then after you're fully onboarded, you know, that's when it gets fun for our team, because that's when we really get to see the data, we get to respond to the data accordingly, make tweaks and make improvements.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Over time. So after you're fully onboarded. Then we're meeting once a month for strategy calls. We're sending you reports with detailed analytics. Once a month, we are refreshing ad creatives.

